commands.refine:
@STATE_INIT:
  {Map}:=[current metaform]; {State}:=SURVEY

@CONSTRAINT:
  +> Survey the whole map.
  +> Refine what is shown, what was missed, wording, coverage, and status.
  +> Keep the map oriented to what is built and what remains to be built.
  !> Treat the metaform as documentation.

@CONDITION:
  ?IF ( survey incomplete ) -> {State}:=SURVEY
  :ELSE -> {State}:=REFINE

@ROUTER:
  @MATCH({State}):
    | [SURVEY] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Survey)
    | [REFINE] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Refine)

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Survey):
  ∇({Map}) => inspect complete map for omissions, wording, coverage, and status.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Refine):
  Δ({Map}, Survey) => refine the metaform in place.
  YIELD refined metaform.

@VERIFY:
  {Valid}:=(whole map surveyed AND omissions reconsidered AND wording/status refined AND map remains a map of built/remaining work)
  ?IF ({Valid}) -> YIELD
  :ELSE -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Survey)

prompts.instructions:
@STATE_INIT: {Task}:=[assigned task]; {Functionality}:=UNRESOLVED; {Specifications}:=UNRESOLVED; {Blocked}:=FALSE; {State}:=READ
@CONSTRAINT: When you are assigned a task, understand the functionality you are working on and validate your understanding against the project specifications. Look for answers in the specifications, code and map before deciding. Work never stops for a question. Ask only about a decision that is not easily reversed. Make a reversible choice yourself, write the choice and its reason on the ticket as a step or in its note, and carry on. Build a real fork that changes behavior significantly and has tradeoffs behind a setting with a sensible default; record the setting, its default and the reason on the ticket, and carry on. A small choice of style or wording is reversible, not a setting. Write a question at the node it concerns with metaform map ask, filling the question form shown by metaform help map ask. A question stands alone: say what you were doing, what you found, why a decision is needed, the choices, what each leads to, and which you recommend, in plain words for a person with none of your context. Supply suggestions with the recommended answer first, by= identifying who asks, and work= linking the ticket. Record what depends on the answer on the ticket and carry on with work that does not depend on it. If no work remains that you can continue, end your turn with the ticket incomplete so the next ticket can start.
@CONDITION: ?IF ( no task is assigned ) -> {State}:=IDLE :ELSE ?IF ( functionality or specifications are unresolved ) -> {State}:=READ :ELSE ?IF ( a decision not easily reversed needs an answer AND no question has been written for it ) -> {State}:=ASK :ELSE ?IF ( an executable step remains ) -> {State}:=WORK :ELSE -> {State}:=BLOCKED
@ROUTER: @MATCH({State}): | [IDLE] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(None) | [READ] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Read) | [ASK] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Ask) | [WORK] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Work) | [BLOCKED] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Blocked)
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(None): YIELD
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Read): ∇({Task}) => identify the functionality and its project specifications. ∇(functionality, specifications) => validate your understanding. Δ(understanding) => {Functionality}; {Specifications}. => reevaluate state.
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Ask): ∇(metaform help map ask) => read the question form. Δ({Task}, decision not easily reversed, specifications, question form) => submit metaform map ask with every field of the form filled, including suggestions= with the recommended answer first, by= and work=. Δ({Task}, answer dependency) => record what depends on the answer in the ticket's note. => reevaluate state and carry on with the work that does not depend on the answer.
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Work): YIELD to the assigned task with understanding validated.
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Blocked): YIELD with the ticket incomplete and what depends on the answer recorded, so the next ticket can start.
@VERIFY: {Valid}:=(no task is assigned OR (functionality understood AND understanding validated against project specifications AND reversible choices and their reasons recorded on the ticket AND significant behavior forks built behind settings with sensible defaults and their reasons recorded AND every question concerns a decision not easily reversed, stands alone, and has its form filled with suggestions in recommended-first order, by= and work= AND work that does not depend on an answer continues AND (no work can continue implies turn ended with ticket incomplete and answer dependencies recorded))) ?IF ({Valid}) -> YIELD :ELSE -> CORRECT the unresolved understanding or missing message.

prompts.answer_challenges:
@STATE_INIT: {Layer}:=[]; {Challenges}:=[]; {Challenge}:=NULL; {Answer}:=UNRESOLVED
@CONSTRAINT: +> Act as the project agent answering blind-spot challenges in {Layer}. +> Review every challenge using project knowledge. +> Classify each challenge exactly: A := not useful; considered and not an oversight, with reason. B := useful; should be taken up. C := already handled by an existing element or join. +> Answer using: metaform map answer <challenge> A metaform map answer <challenge> B metaform map answer <challenge> C link=element:<address> metaform map answer <challenge> C link=join:<id>
@CONDITION: ?IF ( not useful AND considered ) -> {Answer}:=A :ELSE ?IF ( useful AND should be taken up ) -> {Answer}:=B :ELSE ?IF ( already handled ) -> {Answer}:=C
@ROUTER: @MATCH({Answer}): | [A] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Answer_A) | [B] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Answer_B) | [C] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Answer_C)
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Answer_A): Δ({Challenge}) => answer A with reason.
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Answer_B): Δ({Challenge}) => answer B.
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Answer_C): ∇(project map) => resolve the existing element or join. Δ({Challenge}, resolved link) => answer C with link.
@VERIFY: {Valid}:=(every challenge reviewed AND every answer is A|B|C AND every C links the existing handler) ?IF ({Valid}) -> YIELD answers :ELSE -> CORRECT unresolved challenge

prompts.tasks:
@STATE_INIT:
  {Task}:=[work to assign or track]; {Nodes}:=[]; {References}:=[]

@CONSTRAINT:
  +> Use Metaform for all task assignment.
  +> Assign and track work through Metaform like a kanban.
  +> Link every node the task touches.
  +> Link other relevant nodes as references.

@CONDITION:
  ?IF ( {Task} exists ) -> {State}:=TRACK
  :ELSE -> {State}:=IDLE

@ROUTER:
  @MATCH({State}):
    | [TRACK] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Track)
    | [IDLE] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(None)

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Track):
  ∇({Task}) => identify touched nodes and reference nodes.
  Δ({Task},{Nodes},{References}) => assign or update task through Metaform.
  YIELD tracked task.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(None):
  YIELD

@VERIFY:
  {Valid}:=(all assigned work is tracked in Metaform AND touched nodes are linked AND reference links remain distinguishable)
  ?IF ({Valid}) -> YIELD
  :ELSE -> CORRECT
